From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Tue May  4 21:35:38 2004
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Tue, 04 May 2004 22:35:38 +0100
Subject: Re: Converting from correlation to covariance
In-Reply-To: <s097c16a.059@gwia.unt.edu>
References: <s097c16a.059@gwia.unt.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0405042229400.9246-100000@gannet.stats>

outer(sds, sds) * cormatrix

You can see the reverse in several places, e.g. factanal which has

        scale <- sqrt(diag(cmat))
        cmat <- cmat/scale * rep(1/scale, rep.int(p, p))

so  cormatrix *sds * rep(sds, rep.int(p, p))  would be another way.

Example:
library(MASS)
X <- mvrnorm(100, c(0,0), matrix(c(3,1,1,2),2,2))
var(X)
cr <- cor(X); sds <- sqrt(diag(var(X)))
outer(sds, sds) * cr

