Depending exactly what you mean, this is most likely the first principal 
component of (x, y), so princomp is the tool.

I think you are referring to minimizing the sum of squares from the 
points to the fitted lines (orthogonally, not vertically), but, BTW, that 
is not `regression' as normally defined. I have heard this called `total 
least squares' as well as many other things.

