There are two ways you get the boxplot you want.

For your example:

y1<-rnorm(10,0,1)
y2<-rnorm(10,1,1)
y3<-rnorm(10,3,1)

Simply type:

>boxplot(y1,y2,y3)

Or define:

y.data<-c(y1,y2,y3)

group.data<-c(rep(1,10),rep(2,10),rep(3,10))

> boxplot(split(y.data,group.data))

Stephen Smith 

